    "description": "Red de Carreteras de Occidente operates concessioned toll roads and related mobility services in western and central Mexico. Its customers are passenger and freight users moving through one of the country's main industrial and logistics corridors. The operating model is asset-heavy and concession based, with cash flow generated from toll collection and associated road services over long asset lives. Recent company materials describe more than 1,100 kilometers of managed highways, while transaction materials at the time of the Abertis and GIC acquisition described the asset as one of Mexico's largest motorway operators. RCO was constituted in 2007, and Abertis and GIC completed the acquisition of 72.3% of the company in 2020, with GIC disclosed at 21% of the equity.",
